  "slug": "cell-single-cell-66e7",
  "summary": "Single-cell and spatial foundation models are moving from transcriptomics alone toward paired chromatin, splicing, and histology inputs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is representation learning that extends single-cell transcriptomics with additional modalities or priors. Several preprints add chromatin, splicing, or histology inputs: ChromaPert combines paired control RNA-ATAC features for cell-state-dependent perturbation prediction, Crecerelle embeds gene expression with alternative splicing isoforms, and ASTRA performs zero-shot spatial super-resolution from histology and measured RNA. Published work follows similar lines, including unpaired scRNA-ATAC integration with regulatory gene-peak priors (scHPGT), multi-omics clustering with uncertainty weighting (scURL), and mixture-of-experts beta-VAE integration (UniVI). A notable counterpoint is that histology supervision did not yield consistent gains for transcriptomic foundation models, and pretrained gene embeddings transfer mean expression more broadly than spatial patterns. What is new is less architectural novelty than explicit tests of which inputs and priors actually transfer.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-07"
}
